  <main class="prompt-area">
    <!-- ══ CONTEXT REFERENCE ══ -->
    <div id="context" style="scroll-margin-top: 80px;">
      <div class="section-header">
        <span class="section-title">Financial Crime Context Reference</span>
        <span class="section-count">Paste at the top of any session</span>
      </div>

      <div class="context-card">
        <div>
          <h2>Why this file exists</h2>
          <p>Paste this context block at the start of any AI session to ground responses in the regulatory, domain, and platform specifics of financial crime investigations. It prevents generic agile outputs and ensures every story, epic, or comm reflects real compliance obligations.</p>
          <p style="color:#c8a060; font-family:'DM Mono',monospace; font-size:0.72rem; letter-spacing:0.05em;">↓ Copy the block on the right into your prompt before anything else</p>
          <button class="btn-copy" style="margin-top:1rem" onclick="copyContext()">
            <svg width="12" height="12" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5"><rect x="9" y="9" width="13" height="13" rx="2" ry="2"/><path d="M5 15H4a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V4a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h9a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v1"/></svg>
            COPY CONTEXT BLOCK
          </button>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="context-block" id="contextBlock">## FINANCIAL CRIME INVESTIGATIONS PLATFORM — AI SESSION CONTEXT

**Platform Identity**
You are assisting a product team building the Financial Crime Investigations Platform (FCIP) at a tier-1 multinational bank. FCIP is a pure investigation layer — it consumes structured DetectionEvents from upstream detection systems (transaction monitoring, screening, fraud engines) rather than performing detection itself. The commercial position is "bring your own detection."

**Regulatory Frameworks in Scope**
- UK: POCA 2002, Terrorism Act 2000, MLRs 2017, JMLSG Guidance, NCA SAR/DAML regime, FCA SYSC
- EU/Global: FATF 40 Recommendations, 6AMLD, EBA AML/CFT Guidelines, FATF Travel Rule
- US: BSA, FinCEN SAR XML 2.0 schema, OFAC SDN sanctions
- APAC: MAS Notice SFA/FAA (Singapore), AUSTRAC, regional STR obligations

**Core Domain Terminology**
