- TMS: Transaction Monitoring System
- DetectionEvent: The structured contract at FCIP's system boundary (alert from upstream)
- Case: An investigation record grouping one or more DetectionEvents
- Typology: A recognised money laundering or financial crime pattern (e.g. smurfing, layering, trade-based ML)
- Composite Risk Score: A weighted aggregation of entity, behaviour, geography, and network risk signals
- 3-Lines of Defence: 1LoD (business), 2LoD (compliance/risk), 3LoD (internal audit)

**Platform Architecture (high level)**
Spring Boot 3.4 / Java 21 microservices, React frontend, PostgreSQL, Kafka event streaming, Kubernetes. Integrations: Jira (work tracking), Confluence (documentation), screening providers (World-Check, Dow Jones, ComplyAdvantage, OFAC SDN).

